      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Genome editing was achieved by delivering a modified Cas9 nuclease complex, pre-loaded with a specific guide RNA, utilizing adeno-associated virus serotype 9 (AAV9) vectors. Hematopoietic stem cells were subjected to electroporation to introduce the ribonucleoprotein complex into the cellular milieu. Following transduction, cells underwent *in vitro* expansion in cytokine-supplemented media to ensure sufficient target cell yield prior to autologous transplantation. This optimized protocol ensures precise *in vivo* modification of the target HBB locus.",
