      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that looks pretty solid and stays focused on the science. \n\nI just ran it through our internal audit tool to see where we stand before the final draft. The technical density score came back a bit lower than I was hoping for—it's hovering around a 12.4, and for this specific tier of funding, we usually see successful applications scoring 25 or higher.\n\nCould you try expanding this section a bit? We need more detail on the molecular mechanisms and the specific biochemical environments. Try to beef up the technicality to get that score higher, but again, keep it scientifically rigorous. I really don't want it to become a \"word salad\" of buzzwords, it still needs to make sense to a human reviewer.",
